  attempt.
- charts.js appears in no manifest under .swarm/manifests/ at all, and not in
  .swarm/manifests/W4.4.files (five paths, all Go/dashboard templates).
- Ruling 2026-08-29c (user, later and more specific than 29a) reopened attempt 4 for
  "the Budget card's container tint AND headline consume the shared BudgetVerdict
  classification ... + the five kpis.html trim markers. Nothing else." Every named item is
  done and verified by all three lanes, including the objector.

RULING
The finding is not correct as stated (wrong figure identity, wrong worked example, wrong
causal account), and the surface it names is pre-existing, out of the attempt's written
scope, and would not be repaired by the remedy the FAIL implies. It does not render this
attempt's work a failure. OVERRULE.

Record for backlog (a real defect, correctly re-characterised): the Budget card's
sparkline can contradict the card's own headline by hundreds of dollars in either
direction — green tail while the card reads "$300 over", green tail at delta 0 — because
CombinedCumulativeBalance uses whole transaction-months capped at six while
CombinedCumulativeDelta uses fractional MonthsInRange over the selected range. That is a
metrics-basis bug in a separate file (metrics.go / charts.js), materially bigger than the
$1 dead band, and it deserves its own task rather than a fifth W4 attempt.
